# Dependencies
node_modules/
# …and the same name WITHOUT the trailing slash. A trailing slash matches
# DIRECTORIES ONLY, so a `node_modules` SYMLINK (mode 120000) is a file and the
# pattern above never applied to it. Three separate tasks in one sprint created
# such symlinks — pointing at a sibling checkout, to make typecheck/build run in
# a git worktree — and one of them was committed, because `git status` showed it
# as an ordinary new file and `git check-ignore` returned nothing. On a CI runner
# the symlink then occupies the path pnpm must create:
#   ENOENT: no such file or directory, mkdir '.../packages/db/node_modules'
node_modules
.pnpm-store

